    createStaticVNode('<h1 id="_8-ultrasonic-sensor" tabindex="-1">8. Ultrasonic Sensor <a class="header-anchor" href="#_8-ultrasonic-sensor" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;8. Ultrasonic Sensor&quot;">​</a></h1><h2 id="_8-1-introduction" tabindex="-1">8.1 Introduction <a class="header-anchor" href="#_8-1-introduction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;8.1 Introduction&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This section introduces the glowy ultrasonic sensor, an illuminated distance measurement module powered by an industrial-grade ultrasonic chip. The chip integrates ultrasonic transmission, reception, and digital processing circuits. It communicates via I2C to deliver accurate distance measurements.</p><img loading="lazy" height="304" width="455" src="' + _imports_0 + '" class="common_img" style="width:300px;"><h2 id="_8-2-technical-specifications" tabindex="-1">8.2 Technical Specifications <a class="header-anchor" href="#_8-2-technical-specifications" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;8.2 Technical Specifications&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:center;">Parameter</th><th style="text-align:center;">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:center;">Operating voltage</td><td style="text-align:center;">5 V</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">Operating frequency</td><td style="text-align:center;">40 kHz</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">Effective range</td><td style="text-align:center;">2 cm ~ 400 cm</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">Detection angle</td><td style="text-align:center;">15°</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">Display colors</td><td style="text-align:center;">RGB colors</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">Connector model</td><td style="text-align:center;">5264-4AW</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">Mounting compatibility</td><td style="text-align:center;">LEGO-compatible hole spacing</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">Dimensions</td><td style="text-align:center;">55.4 × 23.4 × 27.2 mm</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="_8-3-hands-on-project-1" tabindex="-1">8.3 Hands-On Project 1 <a class="header-anchor" href="#_8-3-hands-on-project-1" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;8.3 Hands-On Project 1&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_8-3-1-project-introduction" tabindex="-1">8.3.1 Project Introduction <a class="header-anchor" href="#_8-3-1-project-introduction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;8.3.1 Project Introduction&quot;">​</a></h3><p>This project uses the ultrasonic sensor to measure obstacle distance. The program continuously reads distance values and prints them to the serial port. Moving obstacles toward or away from the sensor demonstrates the distance measurement principle through live data changes in the serial monitor.</p><h3 id="_8-3-2-hardware-wiring" tabindex="-1">8.3.2 Hardware Wiring <a class="header-anchor" href="#_8-3-2-hardware-wiring" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;8.3.2 Hardware Wiring&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Connect the ultrasonic sensor to port <strong>A</strong> of the controller using a 4-pin module cable.</li></ul><img loading="lazy" height="379" width="1040" src="' + _imports_1 + '" class="common_img" style="width:500px;"><div class="note custom-block github-alert"><p class="custom-block-title">NOTE</p><p></p><p><strong>This sensor supports connection to any port among A, B, C, or D on the controller. Ensure that the port selected in the program matches the physical wiring.</strong></p></div><h3 id="_8-3-3-adding-extensions" tabindex="-1">8.3.3 Adding Extensions <a class="header-anchor" href="#_8-3-3-adding-extensions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;8.3.3 Adding Extensions&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Select <strong>Ultrasonic sensor</strong> under the <strong>Input Module</strong> category.</li></ul><img loading="lazy" height="1040" width="1920" src="' + _imports_2 + '" class="common_img" style="width:800px;"><h3 id="_8-3-4-complete-program-and-analysis" tabindex="-1">8.3.4 Complete Program and Analysis <a class="header-anchor" href="#_8-3-4-complete-program-and-analysis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;8.3.4 Complete Program and Analysis&quot;">​</a></h3><ol><li><p>Upon start-up, initialize the ultrasonic sensor on port A.</p></li><li><p>Inside the main program loop, continuously read the obstacle distance from the ultrasonic sensor on port A.</p></li><li><p>Print the measured distance to the serial port.</p></li><li><p>Add a 0.5-second wait to slow down the serial refresh rate for steady data observation.</p></li></ol><img loading="lazy" height="400" width="610" src="' + _imports_3 + '" class="common_img" style="width:500px;"><div class="note custom-block github-alert"><p class="custom-block-title">NOTE</p><p></p><p><strong>The source files are available for download under <a href="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1fLfLXEVjSMZdojOq7C44xJqZIBm4MDem?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Program Files/ 08-1 Ultrasonic Sensor.sb3</a>.</strong></p></div><h3 id="_8-3-5-program-upload" tabindex="-1">8.3.5 Program Upload <a class="header-anchor" href="#_8-3-5-program-upload" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;8.3.5 Program Upload&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Click <strong>Connect device</strong>, select the serial port, then click the upload button. Wait for the upload success notification to complete the program transfer.</li></ul><img loading="lazy" height="360" width="640" src="' + _imports_4 + '" class="common_img" style="width:800px;"><h3 id="_8-3-6-program-outcome" tabindex="-1">8.3.6 Program Outcome <a class="header-anchor" href="#_8-3-6-program-outcome" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;8.3.6 Program Outcome&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Once the program uploads, check the serial monitor in the lower-right corner of the programming software. Moving an object toward or away from the sensor updates the distance reading. Closer objects produce smaller values. Further objects produce larger values.</p><img loading="lazy" height="956" width="1458" src="' + _imports_5 + '" class="common_img" style="width:800px;"><h2 id="_8-4-hands-on-project-2" tabindex="-1">8.4 Hands-On Project 2 <a class="header-anchor" href="#_8-4-hands-on-project-2" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;8.4 Hands-On Project 2&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_8-4-1-project-introduction" tabindex="-1">8.4.1 Project Introduction <a class="header-anchor" href="#_8-4-1-project-introduction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;8.4.1 Project Introduction&quot;">​</a></h3><p>This project uses the onboard RGB LEDs of the ultrasonic sensor to create an animated light sequence. The LEDs switch from red to green, enter random color mode, flash blue, and finally turn off. The entire sequence loops continuously.</p><h3 id="_8-4-2-hardware-wiring" tabindex="-1">8.4.2 Hardware Wiring <a class="header-anchor" href="#_8-4-2-hardware-wiring" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;8.4.2 Hardware Wiring&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Connect the ultrasonic sensor to port <strong>A</strong> of the controller using a 4-pin module cable.</li></ul><img loading="lazy" height="379" width="1040" src="' + _imports_1 + '" class="common_img" style="width:500px;"><div class="note custom-block github-alert"><p class="custom-block-title">NOTE</p><p></p><p><strong>This sensor supports connection to any port among A, B, C, or D on the controller. Ensure that the port selected in the program matches the physical wiring.</strong></p></div><h3 id="_8-4-3-adding-extensions" tabindex="-1">8.4.3 Adding Extensions <a class="header-anchor" href="#_8-4-3-adding-extensions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;8.4.3 Adding Extensions&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Select <strong>Ultrasonic sensor</strong> under the <strong>Input Module</strong> category.</li></ul><img loading="lazy" height="1040" width="1920" src="' + _imports_2 + '" class="common_img" style="width:800px;"><h3 id="_8-4-4-complete-program-and-analysis" tabindex="-1">8.4.4 Complete Program and Analysis <a class="header-anchor" href="#_8-4-4-complete-program-and-analysis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;8.4.4 Complete Program and Analysis&quot;">​</a></h3><ol><li><p>Upon start-up, initialize the ultrasonic sensor on port A.</p></li><li><p>Inside the main program loop, continuously run the lighting sequence:</p><ul><li><p>Set all sensor LEDs to red and wait 1 second.</p></li><li><p>Set all sensor LEDs to green and wait 1 second.</p></li><li><p>Switch the sensor to random color mode, set LEDs 1 and 2 to flash blue with a 1-second period, and wait 2 seconds.</p></li><li><p>Turn off all sensor LEDs and wait 1 second before repeating the sequence.</p></li></ul></li></ol><img loading="lazy" height="813" width="662" src="' + _imports_6 + '" class="common_img" style="width:500px;"><div class="note custom-block github-alert"><p class="custom-block-title">NOTE</p><p></p><p><strong>The source files are available for download under <a href="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1fLfLXEVjSMZdojOq7C44xJqZIBm4MDem?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Program Files/ 08-2 Ultrasonic Sensor.sb3</a>.</strong></p></div><h3 id="_8-4-5-program-upload" tabindex="-1">8.4.5 Program Upload <a class="header-anchor" href="#_8-4-5-program-upload" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;8.4.5 Program Upload&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Click <strong>Connect device</strong>, select the serial port, then click the upload button. Wait for the upload success notification to complete the program transfer.</li></ul><img loading="lazy" height="360" width="640" src="' + _imports_4 + '" class="common_img" style="width:800px;"><h3 id="_8-4-6-program-outcome" tabindex="-1">8.4.6 Program Outcome <a class="header-anchor" href="#_8-4-6-program-outcome" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;8.4.6 Program Outcome&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Once the program runs, the LEDs on the ultrasonic sensor light up red, then change to green. Next, the sensor enters random color mode with LEDs 1 and 2 flashing blue. Finally, all LEDs turn off for 1 second before the animation repeats.</p>', 45)
